# RISE website — environment variables
#
# All values are optional. Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and
# set what you need. Never commit real secrets — only this example file is
# tracked.
#
# Forms persist to Postgres (via Drizzle ORM) when DATABASE_URL is set below,
# and fall back to a local filesystem store (`data/`, git-ignored) otherwise.
# Resend (email), Sanity (content), and Turnstile (spam protection) swap in
# later behind their seams.

# Postgres connection. When DATABASE_URL is set, the app uses Drizzle over a
# direct Postgres connection (Supabase's transaction pooler, port 6543) for the
# submission store and the notifications audit log. The app disables prepared
# statements, which the transaction pooler requires. Keep this server-side only:
# never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never expose it to the browser. When it
# is unset, the data store falls back to the filesystem.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<host>:6543/postgres

# Optional direct/session connection (port 5432), used only by drizzle-kit for
# migrations (`npm run db:migrate`). Not used by the running app.
# DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<host>:5432/postgres

# Where the filesystem store writes its data (only used when DATABASE_URL is unset).
# Defaults to `./data`.
# RISE_DATA_DIR=

# Recipient recorded on new-submission notifications.
# RISE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=

# Secret that signs admin session cookies. The admin area is disabled (404)
# when this is unset. Use a high-entropy value (32+ random characters); it is
# independent of any account password, so rotating a password does not log
# everyone out, and rotating this secret invalidates all sessions.
# ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=
#
# Admin accounts (with per-account passwords and roles) are NOT set here; create
# the first one from the command line, then manage the rest in the admin UI:
#   node --env-file-if-exists=.env.local scripts/create-admin.mjs
#   (or: npm run create-admin)
# The first/bootstrap account should be a superadmin (the default).
